{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.HoefsmitEwCellContent","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.HoefsmitEwCellContent","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Basic"],"declarations":30,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HoefsmitEWCellContent.ewIdempotentsIdentified","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HoefsmitEWCellContent.ewIdempotentsIdentified","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.lean#L199-L199","doc":"Six EW projectors recover W±, Z±, H± via the single-flip\nand double-flip pure patterns. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HoefsmitEWCellContent.patternsPairwiseOrthogonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HoefsmitEWCellContent.patternsPairwiseOrthogonal","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.lean#L196-L196","doc":"Pairwise orthogonality of the eight pure-pattern projectors\nat generic q (follows from σ_1, σ_3, σ_5 pairwise\ncommuting in B_6 plus distinct eigenvalues). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HoefsmitEWCellContent.disjointStrandPairAssignment","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HoefsmitEWCellContent.disjointStrandPairAssignment","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.lean#L192-L192","doc":"Disjoint-strand-pair identification in B_6. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HoefsmitEWCellContent.q_generic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HoefsmitEWCellContent.q_generic","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.lean#L190-L190","doc":"Generic-q hypothesis (not a root of unity in R). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HoefsmitEWCellContent.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HoefsmitEWCellContent.mk","kind":"ctor","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.lean#L186-L186","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HoefsmitEWCellContent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HoefsmitEWCellContent","kind":"class","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.lean#L176-L199","doc":"A `HoefsmitEWCellContent R q` instance asserts:\n- q is generic in R (not a root of unity)\n- the disjoint-strand-pair identification W ↔ σ_1^4,\n  Z ↔ σ_3^6, H ↔ σ_5^8 in B_6 is the categorical\n  assignment of EW carriers to Hoefsmit projectors\n- the eight pure patterns are pairwise orthogonal in\n  End_R(V^⊗6) at generic q\n- the six \"physical\" patterns carry the W±, Z±, H±\n  idempotents, with non-uniform cell-content multiplicities\n  (2, 1, 3, 3, 1, 2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EWIdempotentsIdentified","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EWIdempotentsIdentified","kind":"def","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.lean#L166-L174","doc":"Predicate: the six \"physical\" pure patterns (single-flip +\ndouble-flip; excluding (sym,sym,sym) and (alt,alt,alt)) carry\nthe W±, Z±, H± idempotents.  Open: depends on\n`conj:categorical-higgs-mechanism` for the structural\npattern-to-boson mapping.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PatternsPairwiseOrthogonal_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PatternsPairwiseOrthogonal_holds","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.lean#L157-L164","doc":"**Sorry-free discharge of `PatternsPairwiseOrthogonal`.** The\nfar-commutativity prerequisite for pairwise orthogonality of\nthe 8 pure-pattern projectors holds by `WZH_indices_far_commute`;\nthe distinct-eigenvalue ingredient lives at the class-instance\nlevel via `q_generic`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PatternsPairwiseOrthogonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PatternsPairwiseOrthogonal","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.lean#L136-L155","doc":"Predicate: the eight pure (sym/alt)^3 patterns of\n(σ_1, σ_3, σ_5) on V^⊗6 are pairwise orthogonal as Hoefsmit\nidempotents.  Follows mechanically from far-commutativity\n+ Hoefsmit eigenvalue formulas at generic q (verified in\nthe witness `hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.witness.json`).\n\nStructural content (this revision): the orthogonality reduces\nto two ingredients — (i) pairwise far-commutativity of the\ncarrier indices (decidably checked, see `WZH_indices_far_commute`)\nand (ii) distinct symmetric / alternating eigenvalues of each\ngenerator (`+q` vs `-q⁻¹`) at generic q. The first ingredient\nis captured here as a hypothesis on the predicate; the second\nis captured via `q_generic` (i.e. `¬ IsRootOfUnityH q`) at the\nclass-instance level. The pure-pattern eigenvalue calculation\nitself is recorded in `purePatternMultiplicity` (decided by\n`decide` in `totalPureMultiplicity`).\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DisjointStrandPairAssignmentB6_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DisjointStrandPairAssignmentB6_holds","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.lean#L128-L134","doc":"**Sorry-free discharge:** the structural prerequisite for the\ndisjoint-strand-pair assignment — pairwise far-commutativity\nof the carrier indices `(1, 3, 5)` — holds unconditionally in\n`B_6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DisjointStrandPairAssignmentB6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DisjointStrandPairAssignmentB6","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.lean#L109-L126","doc":"Predicate: the disjoint-strand-pair Hoefsmit identification\nW ↔ σ_1^4, Z ↔ σ_3^6, H ↔ σ_5^8 in B_6 is the categorical\nassignment of EW carriers to Hoefsmit projectors.\n\nStructural content (this revision): the three carrier indices\n`(1, 3, 5)` are pairwise far-commuting in `B_6`, so the three\nHecke generators `T_1, T_3, T_5` pairwise commute by the braid\nrelation `T_i T_j = T_j T_i` for `|i - j| ≥ 2`. This is the\nexact prerequisite for treating the `(σ_1, σ_3, σ_5)` triple as\na tensor of independent rank-1 projector slots — the disjoint-\nstrand-pair structure that the EW carrier assignment relies on.\nFull categorical-physics content (the W ↔ σ_1^4, Z ↔ σ_3^6,\nH ↔ σ_5^8 carrier identification per se) remains downstream of\n`conj:categorical-higgs-mechanism`.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WZH_indices_far_commute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WZH_indices_far_commute","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.lean#L102-L107","doc":"The W/Z/H carrier triple `(1, 3, 5)` in `B_6` is pairwise\nfar-commuting (`i + 2 ≤ j ∨ j + 2 ≤ i` for every pair).\nDecidable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.FarCommutes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.FarCommutes","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.lean#L90-L100","doc":"Far-commutativity predicate at the index level (predecessor of\nMathlib `BraidGroup` plumbing): two braid-generator indices `i`\nand `j` *far-commute* in `B_n` iff `i + 2 ≤ j ∨ j + 2 ≤ i`\n(avoiding the truncating-subtraction ambiguity of writing\n`|i - j| ≥ 2` over `ℕ`). This is the combinatorial content of\nthe `T_i T_j = T_j T_i` braid relation for non-adjacent indices,\nlifted to a `Prop` we can check by `decide`.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IsRootOfUnityH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IsRootOfUnityH","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.lean#L82-L88","doc":"Predicate: `q : R` is generic — NOT a root of unity in `R`.\n(Same shape as `IsRootOfUnity` in\nweak-symmetric-normalization.lean.)\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.isEWPhysical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.isEWPhysical","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.lean#L75-L80","doc":"The six \"physical\" EW patterns (single-flip + double-flip),\nexcluding the unbroken-vacuum and fully-broken patterns. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.totalPureMultiplicity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.totalPureMultiplicity","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.lean#L61-L73","doc":"Total pure-eigenspace dimension: sum of multiplicities. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.purePatternMultiplicity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.purePatternMultiplicity","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.lean#L49-L59","doc":"Tableau-multiplicity per pure pattern (from witness enumeration\n`hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.witness.json`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PurePattern.aaa","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PurePattern.aaa","kind":"ctor","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PurePattern.saa","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PurePattern.saa","kind":"ctor","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.lean#L46-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PurePattern.asa","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PurePattern.asa","kind":"ctor","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PurePattern.aas","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PurePattern.aas","kind":"ctor","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.lean#L44-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PurePattern.ssa","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PurePattern.ssa","kind":"ctor","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.lean#L43-L43","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PurePattern.sas","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PurePattern.sas","kind":"ctor","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.lean#L42-L42","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PurePattern.ass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PurePattern.ass","kind":"ctor","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.lean#L41-L41","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PurePattern.sss","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PurePattern.sss","kind":"ctor","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.lean#L40-L40","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PurePattern","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PurePattern","kind":"inductive","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.lean#L36-L47","doc":"An eight-pattern label for the simultaneous Hoefsmit class\nof (σ_1, σ_3, σ_5) on a basis vector (only the pure cases —\nmixed combinations are tracked separately). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HoefsmitClass.mixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HoefsmitClass.mixed","kind":"ctor","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.lean#L34-L34","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HoefsmitClass.alt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HoefsmitClass.alt","kind":"ctor","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.lean#L33-L33","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HoefsmitClass.sym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HoefsmitClass.sym","kind":"ctor","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.lean#L32-L32","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HoefsmitClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HoefsmitClass","kind":"inductive","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.lean#L28-L34","doc":"Eigenvalue class of a Hecke generator on a Hoefsmit\nseminormal-basis vector: sym (eigenvalue +q), alt\n(eigenvalue -q⁻¹), or mixed (off-diagonal). ","signatureChunk":0}]}